From 30b77fbacc8dadcd097b3d0370d159eef82e4638 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: SorinS <ssuciu@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 21:54:20 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] --debug: a debug map beside the C, <stem>.debug.json

The C's debug information gives a debugger addresses, lines and C
types, but not what the C types stand for: a resizable is a bare
header, a variable-size value a bare pointer, T& and T? are one pointer
type, bool is u8, a function instance is area_g_2, and a local is in
scope from the function's top (every declaration is hoisted there).
Under --debug the driver now writes, beside the C, a JSON map
(codegen_debugmap.h has its format):

- each function instance: its C name, its Goose qualified name, file
  and lines, and its generic bindings;
- each of its locals and parameters: C name, Goose name, Goose type
  and the lines it is in scope over, from its declaration to the end
  of the innermost block around it;
- each struct and enum those types name: its C name where the program
  has one, and its fields, or its variants with their tags and fields.

The map is collected as the C is generated and changes none of it: C
type names are recorded where NameCT makes them, not asked for.

Test: on seven sample programs the C is byte-identical with and
without the map; every codegen test's map under --debug is valid JSON.
